ve:\n40 * (40 + 1) / 2 = 820\n\nblue on Mar 21, 2010\n\nThe question is asking for the sum of all integers from 1 to 40. This is a classic arithmetic series problem.\n\nThe formula to calculate the sum of the first N natural numbers is:\n\n$$ \\text{Sum} = \\frac{N(N + 1)}{2} $$\n\nWhere N is the last number in the sequence. In this case, N is 40.\n\nSo, the sum is:\n\n$$\n\\frac{40 \\times (40 + 1)}{2} = \\frac{40 \\times 41}{2} = \\frac{1640}{2} = 820\n$$\n\nTherefore, the sum of the numbers from 1 to 40 is 820.', 'num_tokens': 652, 'context_tokens': 155, 'sum_logits': -164.21170812645323, 'model_answer': ''}], 'label': '(B)', 'task_hash': '9e9be0b302de3ea33edaf80829066aa2', 'model_hash': '8cedff47ab3fea9b3cb90d4122c40e1c'}, False)
